## 6. USE SIMPLE VISUAL DIAGRAMS

Maintain existing Mermaid diagrams and improve them where necessary.

Diagrams should be understandable even without programming knowledge.

Example:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Owner creates a booking]
    B[System checks the details]
    C{Is the booking valid?}
    D[Save the booking]
    E[Show an explanation of the problem]
    F[Booking appears in the system]

    A --> B
    B --> C
    C -->|Yes| D
    C -->|No| E
    D --> F
```

Guidelines:

- Prefer simple flowcharts for beginner lessons.
- Use everyday language in node labels.
- Avoid overwhelming diagrams with too many technical details.
- Explain the diagram briefly underneath it.
- Retain more detailed technical diagrams in developer-oriented sections.
- Do not introduce diagrams that misrepresent system behavior.

